change:
  id: CHG-012
  title: Codify bounded model-session and multi-model efficiency
  status: proposed
  intent: Make source-referenced session reuse, explicit multi-model roles, bounded resource use and independent-review reset rules durable and repository-checked agent operating practice.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - SYS-001
    - ARCH-001
    - PAT-002
    - Q-010
    - Q-011
    - RISK-001

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: bounded-model-session-efficiency
    requirement: Agent operations reuse a provider session only for one stable objective, role and permission scope, with a source-referenced durable handoff.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a bounded task continues with the same objective, role and permission scope
        then: it may retain one session identifier and uses compact source-referenced context rather than resending the repository
        and:
          - the repository, specification and handoff remain authoritative
          - cache evidence is recorded only when the provider exposes it
      - id: S2
        when: the objective, role or permission scope changes, an independent review starts, a transport fails, or response reserve is exhausted
        then: a fresh session is required and the reset reason is recorded
        and:
          - an independent reviewer does not inherit an implementer's unreviewed verdict
      - id: S3
        when: work is delegated across model classes
        then: each invocation has an explicit role, bounded context packet and resource envelope
        and:
          - actual token, cache, latency and cost evidence is recorded when available
          - unavailable telemetry is not estimated or invented
      - id: S4
        when: a model route is selected or a retry budget is exhausted
        then: direct user selection wins and repeated blind retries stop after the bounded allowance
        and:
          - automatic provider routing remains deferred pending Q-010 evidence
          - no route changes deterministic validation, fitness, promotion, audit or privacy constraints

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: repo-contract/model-routing-policy-session-reuse-controls
    layer: contract
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: repo-contract/model-routing-policy-session-reset-controls
    layer: contract
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: repo-contract/model-routing-policy-multi-model-budget-controls
    layer: contract
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: repo-contract/model-routing-policy-safety-links
    layer: contract

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: record session lifecycle, resource telemetry and multi-model roles in the coordination policy and AGENTS contract
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: link the durable pattern, profile and user-facing architecture/development guidance to the policy
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: make policy controls repository-checked and validate the structured proposal
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - automatic runtime model/provider routing or cost optimisation
  - provider price assumptions or hidden retry behavior
  - replacing deterministic candidate authority with model judgement

risks:
  - a textual contract check protects presence and links, not empirical provider economics; Q-010 retains the measured-usage and ablation gate
  - a retained session can carry stale conclusions; reset triggers and source revalidation reduce but do not eliminate that risk
